{"name":"Castaway","hex":"#6dbac0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"castaway","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Cast adrift or ashore; marooned.","Shipwrecked."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A shipwrecked sailor.","A discarded person or thing."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/castaway"}],"entries":[{"title":"Castaway","blocks":[{"text":"A castaway is a person who is cast adrift or ashore. While the situation usually happens after a shipwreck, some people voluntarily stay behind on a desert island, either to evade captors or the world in general. A person may also be left ashore as punishment (marooned)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e2/Rescue_by_seamen_of_USNS_Passumpsic.jpg/330px-Rescue_by_seamen_of_USNS_Passumpsic.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Castaway"},{"title":"Castaway (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Castaway is a 1986 biographical-drama film directed by Nicolas Roeg and starring Amanda Donohoe and Oliver Reed. The screenplay was by Allan Scott, adapted from the eponymous 1984 book by Lucy Irvine, telling of her experiences of staying for a year with writer Gerald Kingsland on the isolated island of Tuin, between New Guinea and Australia."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9f/Castawayposter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Castaway_(film)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Desertisland.jpg/500px-Desertisland.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Desertisland.jpg/1280px-Desertisland.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Desertisland.jpg/500px-Desertisland.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Castaways may need to survive on a desert island.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADesertisland.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Robinson_Crusoe_and_Man_Friday_Offterdinger.jpg/330px-Robinson_Crusoe_and_Man_Friday_Offterdinger.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Robinson_Crusoe_and_Man_Friday_Offterdinger.jpg/330px-Robinson_Crusoe_and_Man_Friday_Offterdinger.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Robinson Crusoe (1719) by Daniel Defoe. Illustration of Crusoe standing over Man Friday after freeing him from the cannibals.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARobinson_Crusoe_and_Man_Friday_Offterdinger.jpg"}],"sounds":{"castaway":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/89/En-us-castaway.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/8/89/En-us-castaway.ogg/En-us-castaway.ogg.mp3"}]}}}